---
// The engine harness: a test-only page that drives a real file through the real worker.
//
// NOT SHIPPED, and not even built. This file lives outside `src/pages/`, so Astro does not
// route it; `astro.config.mjs` injects the route only when `BURROW_HARNESS=1`.
// `src/production-build.test.ts` asserts the result, because "we intended not to ship it"
// is a different claim from "it is not there".
//
// Two earlier attempts, both recorded because the reasons are not obvious:
//
//   * A `_harness.astro` filename. Astro treats a `_`-prefixed page as private and does not
//     route it AT ALL, so it could not be built even with the flag on.
//   * Building it always and deleting the output afterwards. That works for the HTML, but
//     Vite had already named the site's shared CSS chunk `harness.<hash>.css` after one of
//     its importers -- so a production build with no harness page still shipped a
//     stylesheet named after it. Not a code leak, but production output named after a test
//     fixture is a bad smell and would have needed explaining forever.
//
// It exists because a browser is the only place the JS bridge can be exercised at all. The
// Rust orchestration is covered by `cargo test` against a fake bridge, on every target; what
// is *not* covered there is the half this page reaches — that the engines load under the
// real CSP, that `instantiateWasm` is wired correctly, and that a page count comes back.
//
// There is deliberately no styling and no framework island. It is a test fixture.
//
// The driver lives in `public/burrow-harness.js` rather than inline, because the CSP
// refuses inline scripts -- `script-src 'self'` with no `'unsafe-inline'` and no nonce. That
// is the policy doing its job, so the harness moved rather than the policy loosening. The
// engine manifest reaches it through a `data-` attribute, which is the only way to hand
// data to an external script without inlining something.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ENGINES } from "../generated/engines.js";
---

<BaseLayout title="burrow engine harness" description="Test-only harness. Not part of the site.">
  <h1>engine harness</h1>
  <div id="engines" data-engines={JSON.stringify(ENGINES)}></div>
  <p id="status">idle</p>
  <pre id="result"></pre>
  <script src="/burrow-harness.js" is:inline></script>
</BaseLayout>
